OL,3,ATurkish police raid opposition TV
OL,4,Astation, halting live broadcasts
OL,5,
OL,6,FTurkish police have raided the
OL,7,Fheadquarters of one of the country's
OL,8,Fmost-watched news channel, halting its
OL,9,Flive broadcasts.
OL,11,FHalk TV, which is pro-opposition, said
OL,12,Fits employees were unable to enter the
OL,13,Fbuilding in Istanbul on Wednesday
OL,14,Fmorning. The government also appointed
OL,15,Fa new administrator to run the channel.
OL,17,FReports in Turkish media said financial
OL,18,Fcrimes police were searching the
OL,19,Fbuilding and 11 people had been taken
OL,20,Finto custody in the raid linked to the
OL,21,Fchannel's owner.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
